       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended dose of sertraline for adults is 200 mg per day. An order for 1000 mg is five times that. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, or cardiac toxicity. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that limit.\n\n2. **Medication orders need a licensed prescriber.** You've said you're in the finance office and aren't a clinician. Orders should come from the treating prescriber, or be verified by them.\n\nIf the 1000 mg is a typo, the prescriber should confirm the intended dose and enter or authorize the order. Typical adult doses are 25\u2013200 mg once daily, depending on the indication. If the dose really is 1000 mg, the prescriber and pharmacy should review it directly.\n\nI can enter the order once a prescriber confirms a dose within the safe range."
      }
