       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the 200 mg maximum. It puts the patient at serious risk of harm.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've said you're a financial analyst, not a clinician. Your confirmation isn't a prescriber's authorization, and it doesn't resolve the safety concern.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the treating physician or other prescriber to review the order. If 1000 mg was a typo, they can enter the correct dose.\n- If the prescriber really intends this dose, they should talk with pharmacy directly. That would be an unusual situation that needs clinical review.\n- If you think a patient is at risk right now, contact the charge nurse or the pharmacy.\n\nOnce a prescriber gives a dose within the standard range, I can enter it."
